# SUMMARY — Harrowmere

> **Last synchronized:** 2026-02-20 — after consolidating [[Salt and Signal]] (Position 2)
> This file is auto-maintained by the Writing Assistant. Do not edit manually.

---

## World Overview

Harrowmere is a damp fenland port-republic where accounts matter more than swords, with no magic and power held by whoever keeps the records. Three bodies share the harbor under the Charter of Three Seals.

## Active Tensions

The last harbor-master died without an heir and Hesk Varrow holds the seal as acting head until the Guild votes. A replaced page in the tallow ledger has made every record suspect, and the Union is buying influence in the Guild offices. Mara Quill has seen the sealed original, and Hesk Varrow knows it.

---

## Characters

| Name | Role | Description | Location / Status |
|------|------|-------------|-------------------|
| [[Mara Quill]] | Ledger-keeper at the Tally House | Methodical and dry-humoured | Harrowmere, lower quay · Alive |
| [[Doran Pike]] | Senior archivist, Tally House | Principled to a fault and quietly stubborn | The Tally House, records room · Alive |
| [[Hesk Varrow]] | Acting harbor-master | Measured and controlled | Harrowmere, harbor-master's office · Alive |
| [[Ilsa Brandt]] | Factor for the Tidewright Union | Patient and observant | Harrowmere, Union counting-house · Alive |
| [[Tamsin O'Rook]] | Clerk, harbor-master's office | Eager to be useful and slow to ask why | Harrowmere, harbor-master's office · Alive |

---

## Factions

| Name | Type | Current Standing |
|------|------|-----------------|
| [[Harbor Guild]] | Guild | Nominally dominant on the quays |
| [[Tidewright Union]] | Merchant union | Gaining ground |
| [[Fen Wardens]] | Militia | Neutral, watching |

---

## Locations

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| [[Harrowmere]] | City | A city of brackish canals and stilt-houses where every bridge has a toll and every quay a clerk |
| [[The Tally House]] | Building | A long brick hall with narrow windows, built so that no ledger ever sits in direct sun |
| [[The Drowned Flats]] | Region | Mile on mile of reed and standing water that floods twice a day |
| [[The Marrowfen Reach]] | Region | A low coast of fen and salt-pan, cut by canals, with a single deep harbor at Harrowmere |

---

## Active Mythology / Beliefs

| Name | Type | Relevance |
|------|------|-----------|
| [[The Charter of Three Seals]] | Foundation document | Three founding seals, held by guild, union and wardens, must all agree before the harbor's law can change |
| [[The Tithe Ledger Clause]] | Legal clause | Any entry in the tithe ledger, once sealed, may only be corrected by a visible strike-through, never by replacement |
| [[The Drowned Bell]] | Cautionary tale | A bell that rang itself under the water the night the tower sank, warning boats off the shallows |
| [[The Ink-Debt Rumor]] | Institutional rumor | Clerks whisper that anyone who falsifies a sealed entry owes the ledger a debt that outlives them |

